R-IN1 R-IN9 R-IN10 R-AP1 R-AP16 R-AD35 R-RG4 R-CV1 R-IX4 R-SP23 R-SP8 R-AP74 R-IN2 R-IN8 R-IN6 R-PD9 (slice 206i, Design Q560): `tln init --platform roc-lang/basic-cli@0.24.0` with a registry (config.toml: `share = false`). The world is share/sh62-no-send-init (the compiler list is the registry list, N = nightly-2026-10-12-2a2a2a2 is downloaded after a person says Enter), with no GitHub list of the platform: the route is gone, so a call to it is a 404.
The platform is read as `add` reads a full name (R-AP1, Q560): the guard (`GET /repos/roc-lang/basic-cli`, no token, `programs gh`), then `GET /v1/packages/roc-lang/basic-cli/releases` (3 releases, the copy `get/<sha256 of the path>`). The named release 0.24.0 is in the list (R-IN9 (2)), so the start header has its URL (R-IN10 (1)). The resolve is the flow of `upgrade roc` (R-IN10 (2), Q560): the platform is held (R-SP23), so the closure query has `groups` [] (as registry/cv1-upgrade-free: "no package is free") and the hash of the named release; the compiler window is the free window of that case (the oldest row, 2026-10-08, to the newest that min-release-age allows, 2026-10-12). One query, the answer has the release and its artifact, no runs. No GitHub list, no archive read for the candidates. The facts query is for 1 hash and the 6 rows of the compiler list (facts=6, as init/it5-version run 8). Then the same ladder as the guard share/sh62-no-send-init: 4 probes, the pin is N, the basic-cli template (R-IN8: the repository decides, not the version). `resolved at log:60` (the `log_size` of the answer).
`share = false`: no queue call, no smoke build, no send (the case is the control of sh62: the same run with sharing off). Written by hand from the pre-change files of sh62 (research/slice-206i-revert/mkcases.py).
